        <body>
            <div xml:id="d301">

                <pb facs="0572" n="472" sameAs="frus:frus1880/pg472"/>

                <head>No. 301.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hoppin to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-12-27"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 27, 1879</date>.
                        (Received January 12.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 128.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to Mr. Welsh’s No. 327, of the
                    29th July last, and to instruction No. 371 of the 15th of September last, upon
                    the method of settling international accounts of extradition expenses, I have
                    the honor to inclose a copy of the correspondence which has taken place upon
                    this subject since the last-mentioned date, between this legation and the
                    foreign office.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>W. J. HOPPIN.</signed></closer>





